s expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1245 AM MDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1141 PM MDT, Gauge reports indicated high stream flows.\nFlooding is already occurring in the warned area.\n- Widespread inundation of agriculture fields, wetlands, and other\nlow-lying areas.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande and West Central\nAlamosa Counties.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-27T00:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4ae14a0d5b0f32c693a127b62408ea7b7418f993.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4ae14a0d5b0f32c693a127b62408ea7b7418f993.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 25 at 9:00AM MDT until October 27 at 9:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall which occurred over\nthe last couple of days is expected or ongoing.\n\n* WHERE...Northeastern Conejos County in south central Colorado...\nSouthwestern Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 900 AM MDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding will occur in low-lying and flood-prone\nlocations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 852 AM MDT, flooding was occurring along the Rio Grande River\nin low lying and agricultural areas. This high water is due to\nall of the heavy rain which occurred over the last couple of\ndays.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include low lying\nareas in parts of Alamosa and parts of Conejos counties.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-27T09:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO; Co